    "title": "Carlsbad 1911",
    "place": "Carlsbad, 20 August – 24 September 1911",
    "story": "Twenty-six masters in a single round robin, 325 games in all. Richard Teichmann, nicknamed 'Richard the Fifth' for his many fifth places, won the tournament of his life. Among the debutants was the 18-year-old Alexander Alekhine.",
